This package is a new extraction of Linux-visible mount, open_tree, clone3
namespace and fsconfig/fsmount policy designed for TheKernel and distributed
under Apache-2.0. It is not a port of any upstream file: no Linux source file
was translated, adapted, or restructured here.

Linux sources were consulted to understand observable mount-flag acceptance,
namespace capability ordering, propagation and attribute rules, and the
fsconfig/fsmount argument grammar. No other upstream was consulted for this
package.

Copied text: Linux C is quoted verbatim in Rust doc comments as the
observable-semantics authority. Measured against the Linux 7.2.3 tree with
`scripts/ci/scan_linux_excerpts.py` (whitespace-normalised lines of >= 40
characters inside fenced code blocks, matched line for line): 7 lines across
3 blocks, all in `src/lib.rs`; at the inclusive >= 25-character threshold 16 lines
across 5 blocks. The hunks are
`fs/namespace.c:4456-4469`, `:4446-4461`, `:3220-3229`, `:2061-2063` and
`:4096-4101`. Every block carries an inline marker line, "Excerpt: Linux
v7.2.3 <file>:<lines> - GPL-2.0-only, (C) The Linux Kernel Authors" - 5 marker
lines at `src/lib.rs:387`, `:418`, `:481`, `:548`, `:567`, so the two hunks a
40-character scan cannot see (`:387`, `:567`) are still attributed by range - in
addition to the file-and-line citation its surrounding prose already gave.

Those fragments are GPL-2.0-only, (C) The Linux Kernel Authors. They are
comment text, not code: no Linux code is linked, assembled, or compiled into
this package, and the Apache-2.0 grant above does not extend to the quoted
text. Nothing else in this package reproduces upstream source text. See
`docs/upstream-provenance.md` for the full per-file index.
